#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10004
#: feda1c5992944ec5bf825a9b4031c745
msgid "Introduction to Understanding Causal Relationships in Media Mix Modeling"
msgstr ""
"Introducción a la comprensión de las relaciones causales en el modelado "
"de mezcla de medios"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10006
#: e96fae2b0a1741a196d4c9c1a1354f36
msgid ""
"Causal identification is about figuring out if we can prove a cause-and-"
"effect relationship using the data we have and our assumptions. This "
"process helps us establish clear links between different factors instead "
"of looking at their correlations. It is essential when working with "
"observational data, which can be affected by hidden factors and biases "
"that make it hard to see true causal relationships."
msgstr ""
"La identificación causal consiste en determinar si podemos probar una "
"relación de causa y efecto utilizando los datos que tenemos y nuestras "
"suposiciones. Este proceso nos ayuda a establecer vínculos claros entre "
"diferentes factores en lugar de centrarnos en sus correlaciones. Es "
"esencial al trabajar con datos observacionales, que pueden verse "
"afectados por factores ocultos y sesgos que dificultan la identificación "
"de verdaderas relaciones causales."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10008
#: cc81a7d233314eac8a27c463e541aaab
msgid ""
"Note: Inspired by the notebook from [Bridging Causal Thinking and Media "
"Mix Models: Carlos Trujillo & Ben "
"Vincent](https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1r5pi9Lh_A6h_CKQFEjyn-"
"7iykL8x-X_H#scrollTo=DRFEJyK1VCi3)."
msgstr ""
"Nota: Inspirado en el cuaderno de [Bridging Causal Thinking and Media Mix"
" Models: Carlos Trujillo & Ben "
"Vincent](https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1r5pi9Lh_A6h_CKQFEjyn-"
"7iykL8x-X_H#scrollTo=DRFEJyK1VCi3)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10010
#: 6cd4c59e08cc489fbbe4a1ede231c18d
msgid "Why Is Understanding Causal Relationships Important in Regressions?"
msgstr ""
"¿Por qué es importante entender las relaciones causales en las "
"regresiones?"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10012
#: c4aee358a19342938ce64bcb1bdcf5ff
msgid ""
"In regression models, we often aim to estimate how one or more factors "
"affect an outcome. However, if we don't consider causality carefully, our"
" estimates can be biased due to:"
msgstr ""
"En los modelos de regresión, a menudo buscamos estimar cómo uno o más "
"factores afectan un resultado. Sin embargo, si no consideramos la "
"causalidad con cuidado, nuestras estimaciones pueden estar sesgadas "
"debido a:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10014
#: 7500c5be80eb40c1bc9e1b1260d0f6c1
msgid ""
"**Confounding Bias**: This happens when a hidden factor influences both "
"the predictor and the outcome, leading to misleading connections."
msgstr ""
"**Sesgo confuso**: Esto ocurre cuando un factor oculto influye tanto en "
"el predictor como en el resultado, lo que lleva a conexiones engañosas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10015
#: ef02aa0faa3e4ead8d7e8b3f7d211a81
msgid ""
"**Selection Bias**: When we use non-random samples, this can distort the "
"estimated relationships."
msgstr ""
"**Sesgo de Selección**: Cuando utilizamos muestras no aleatorias, esto "
"puede distorsionar las relaciones estimadas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10016
#: 15d288f78e5b49f989adfda864ad6c09
msgid ""
"**Overcontrol**: Adjusting for variables that are influenced by the "
"treatment can lead to incorrect estimates of causal effects."
msgstr ""
"**Sobrecontrol**: Ajustar las variables que son influenciadas por el "
"tratamiento puede llevar a estimaciones incorrectas de los efectos "
"causales."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10018
#: 8733f16aa3b74337b3e3ac54f29ba2a9
msgid ""
"Causal identification helps us adjust the right variables in the "
"regression to isolate the true effect by addressing confounders and "
"avoiding unnecessary adjustments. Without it, we can run into several "
"problems:"
msgstr ""
"La identificación causal nos ayuda a ajustar las variables adecuadas en "
"la regresión para aislar el verdadero efecto al abordar los factores de "
"confusión y evitar ajustes innecesarios. Sin ella, podemos enfrentar "
"varios problemas:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10020
#: d5044ad5842a4bbd922ec4d89083f409
msgid ""
"**Bias in Estimates**: Our understanding of effect size and direction "
"might be wrong, which can lead to poor decisions."
msgstr ""
"**Sesgo en las estimaciones**: Nuestra comprensión del tamaño y la "
"dirección del efecto puede ser incorrecta, lo que puede llevar a "
"decisiones equivocadas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10021
#: 6eade91769fe41aca79284677ebd92e0
msgid ""
"**Spurious Correlations**: We might misinterpret coincidental "
"relationships as causal."
msgstr ""
"**Correlaciones Espurias**: Podríamos malinterpretar relaciones "
"coincidentes como causales."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10022
#: 2f05f0134e444927b0d22df319851e2e
msgid ""
"**Inefficient Models**: Including irrelevant variables or missing "
"important confounders can weaken the model’s accuracy and clarity."
msgstr ""
"**Modelos Ineficientes**: Incluir variables irrelevantes o faltar "
"variables de confusión importantes puede debilitar la precisión y "
"claridad del modelo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10024
#: e6f5727d7b3b45f887b86d49ef084700
msgid ""
"In media mix modeling (MMM), where businesses allocate budgets across "
"different channels to maximize returns, these issues can lead to poor "
"resource allocation, wasted money, or misattributing success to "
"ineffective strategies."
msgstr ""
"En la modelización de mezcla de medios (MMM), donde las empresas asignan "
"presupuestos a diferentes canales para maximizar los retornos, estos "
"problemas pueden llevar a una mala asignación de recursos, dinero "
"desperdiciado o a atribuir erróneamente el éxito a estrategias "
"ineficaces."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10026
#: a7285980b2e144bb813934f7ebedd624
msgid "Key Concepts in This Notebook"
msgstr "Conceptos clave en este cuaderno"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10028
#: ef71a077df2c4ed8af8e37743091b913
msgid "This notebook covers key ideas in causal inference, including:"
msgstr "Este cuaderno abarca ideas clave en la inferencia causal, incluyendo:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10030
#: 32131b00a72f4050b4c93b11e44b0ef2
msgid ""
"**Causal Directed Acyclic Graphs (DAGs)**: These are visual tools that "
"show the assumed causal relationships in the data."
msgstr ""
"**Grafos Acíclicos Dirigidos Causales (DAGs)**: Estas son herramientas "
"visuales que muestran las relaciones causales asumidas en los datos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10031
#: 980acc0b4a1c4b6bb4e93c89a511aa91
msgid ""
"**Backdoor Criterion**: This rule helps identify which variables block "
"paths that create misleading connections between the treatment and "
"outcome."
msgstr ""
"**Criterio de Puerta Trasera**: Esta regla ayuda a identificar qué "
"variables bloquean los caminos que crean conexiones engañosas entre el "
"tratamiento y el resultado."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10032
#: eddfcd71d5f7477fb381c60f42a81856
msgid ""
"**Minimal Adjustment Set**: This is the smallest group of factors needed "
"to meet the backdoor criterion, ensuring accurate causal estimates."
msgstr ""
"**Conjunto de Ajuste Mínimo**: Este es el grupo más pequeño de factores "
"necesarios para cumplir con el criterio de puerta trasera, asegurando "
"estimaciones causales precisas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10034
#: fc34c7a9118f470ca1087a29e704b1ca
msgid ""
"These tools help us understand causal inference more clearly and give us "
"solid guidelines for choosing variables in media mix models."
msgstr ""
"Estas herramientas nos ayudan a comprender la inferencia causal de manera"
" más clara y nos brindan pautas sólidas para elegir variables en modelos "
"de mezcla de medios."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10036
#: 98af60d12d084dcdb7bcbdd8afc66555
msgid ""
"By the end of this notebook, you will learn how to use `pymc-marketing` "
"alongside causal thinking principles for effective media mix modeling."
msgstr ""
"Al final de este cuaderno, aprenderá a utilizar `pymc-marketing` junto "
"con los principios del pensamiento causal para un modelado efectivo de la"
" mezcla de medios."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:10038
#: 4fb8db8cf87249ea8ac14d9471381c4e
msgid "Let’s start by importing the necessary libraries!"
msgstr "¡Comencemos importando las bibliotecas necesarias!"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:40002
#: 0d1af23a441747a0ab6e11682c3bf295
msgid "Business problem"
msgstr "Problema empresarial"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:40004
#: 7a7cc680ab8e451c9c9a8358006838eb
msgid ""
"Imagine you run a retail company that advertises its products. You've "
"been in business for a while and have noticed steady sales growth. During"
" holidays, sales increase even more. However, you're not the only one "
"advertising; a competitor is also promoting their products, likely with "
"discounts or special offers."
msgstr ""
"Imagina que diriges una empresa minorista que publicita sus productos. "
"Has estado en el negocio durante un tiempo y has notado un crecimiento "
"constante en las ventas. Durante las festividades, las ventas aumentan "
"aún más. Sin embargo, no eres el único que publicita; un competidor "
"también está promoviendo sus productos, probablemente con descuentos u "
"ofertas especiales."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:40006
#: 6dd3a860a59d45729d53c1d6b0db28ae
msgid "Let's explore how different factors relate to each other:"
msgstr "Exploremos cómo se relacionan entre sí diferentes factores:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:40008
#: 25c080c717e049389151d532aa61b477
msgid ""
"**Christmas (C)**: The holiday season boosts consumer interest, leading "
"to more ad views (X1 and X2) and directly increasing your sales (T)."
msgstr ""
"**Navidad (C)**: La temporada navideña incrementa el interés del "
"consumidor, lo que lleva a más visualizaciones de anuncios (X1 y X2) y "
"aumenta directamente sus ventas (T)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:40009
#: 49bf63f9d65c47d8b3159dea30d7116f
msgid "**Marketing Channels (X1, X2)**:"
msgstr "**Canales de Marketing (X1, X2)**:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:40010
#: 49d367304738417f91bd28b2ae522f68
msgid "**X1**: Social media ads, like those on Facebook or TikTok."
msgstr "**X1**: Anuncios en redes sociales, como los de Facebook o TikTok."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:40011
#: 9975dd0b19f64ade8b0235769c776d0d
msgid ""
"**X2**: Search engine ads, which can enhance the impact of social media "
"ads (these channels work well together)."
msgstr ""
"**X2**: Anuncios en motores de búsqueda, que pueden aumentar el impacto "
"de los anuncios en redes sociales (estos canales funcionan bien juntos)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:40012
#: d9cf358e79044c01b13a81be353e15c1
msgid "**Target (T)**: Your goal is to maximize sales revenue."
msgstr "**Objetivo (T)**: Su meta es maximizar los ingresos por ventas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:40013
#: 584d0fac0b5940fc95aced2e60afb206
msgid "**Unseen Factors**:"
msgstr "**Factores no visibles**:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:40014
#: 4f687cf700e24c6bac3ec458bc156566
msgid ""
"**Competitor Offers (I)**: Your competitor may run aggressive holiday "
"discounts, which could lessen the impact of your search ads (X2) and "
"reduce your sales (T)."
msgstr ""
"**Ofertas de Competidores (I)**: Su competidor puede ofrecer descuentos "
"agresivos durante las festividades, lo que podría disminuir el impacto de"
" sus anuncios de búsqueda (X2) y reducir sus ventas (T)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:40015
#: 168a925f957e44d1b05a212b19bc265c
msgid ""
"**Market Growth (G)**: Economic growth during the holiday season might "
"boost sales (T) regardless of your advertising efforts."
msgstr ""
"**Crecimiento del Mercado (G)**: El crecimiento económico durante la "
"temporada navideña podría impulsar las ventas (T) independientemente de "
"sus esfuerzos publicitarios."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:40017
#: c7bde83260c447b499f81242888172cc
msgid "Visualizing Relationships with a DAG"
msgstr "Visualizando relaciones con un DAG"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:40019
#: 86eeee7b176b4cda9794f364ac9af259
msgid "We can illustrate these ideas using a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG)."
msgstr "Podemos ilustrar estas ideas utilizando un Grafo Acíclico Dirigido (DAG)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:60002
#: ddf756e2f9a549339c03a1ef74f5124e
msgid "Observed Factors:"
msgstr "Factores observados:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:60003
#: fcbad84893d04f43b5850118672c53b2
msgid ""
"**Marketing Impressions X1 and X2**: Two channels (search ads and social "
"ads) that can affect sales (T). They can also impact each other."
msgstr ""
"**Impresiones de Marketing X1 y X2**: Dos canales (anuncios de búsqueda y"
" anuncios en redes sociales) que pueden afectar las ventas (T). También "
"pueden influirse mutuamente."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:60004
#: 5b27de68efd74cd880ea4d0d54e6c3a9
msgid "**Target (T)**: The key metric you want to improve, like sales revenue."
msgstr ""
"**Objetivo (T)**: La métrica clave que desea mejorar, como los ingresos "
"por ventas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:60006
#: 0e6eca478ac745ed9405e65644836c98
msgid "Unseen Factors (Dashed Elements):"
msgstr "Factores no visibles (Elementos discontinuos):"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:60007
#: 61c9329388d546e5a7512482b5c373f8
msgid ""
"**Christmas (C)**: A seasonal event that influences both marketing "
"impressions (X1, X2) and sales (T)."
msgstr ""
"**Navidad (C)**: Un evento estacional que influye tanto en las "
"impresiones de marketing (X1, X2) como en las ventas (T)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:60008
#: 6680f508f70541aaaa28e5e21c72232c
msgid ""
"**Competitor Offers (I)**: Actions by competitors, such as discounts, "
"which can influence marketing channels and sales."
msgstr ""
"**Ofertas de Competidores (I)**: Acciones de los competidores, como "
"descuentos, que pueden influir en los canales de marketing y en las "
"ventas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:60009
#: f205ba8733ed4321a459c8c54a179d85
msgid "**Market Growth (G)**: Broader economic trends that affect sales."
msgstr ""
"**Crecimiento del Mercado (G)**: Tendencias económicas más amplias que "
"afectan las ventas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:60011
#: 08e6f052926d4ba59c3bf685e2e41584
msgid ""
"Note: Dashed elements are not possible to intervene, on the other hand, "
"solid elements are possible to intervene."
msgstr ""
"Nota: Los elementos en línea discontinua no se pueden intervenir, "
"mientras que los elementos en línea continua sí se pueden intervenir."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:60013
#: 390ccb3d5db241c8bc7ef9f06d6c7bbb
msgid "Key Relationships:"
msgstr "Relaciones Clave:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:60014
#: 57609e85e927470c854f3f6b63ad908c
msgid ""
"Christmas (C) boosts both marketing impressions (X1, X2) and directly "
"increases sales (T) during the holiday season."
msgstr ""
"La Navidad (C) impulsa tanto las impresiones de marketing (X1, X2) como "
"aumenta directamente las ventas (T) durante la temporada navideña."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:60015
#: 52660624f3424c99ae4709b9594516cc
msgid ""
"Marketing impressions (X1, X2) affect sales (T) through your advertising "
"efforts. X1 can help X2 (e.g., social ads support search ads)."
msgstr ""
"Las impresiones de marketing (X1, X2) afectan las ventas (T) a través de "
"sus esfuerzos publicitarios. X1 puede ayudar a X2 (por ejemplo, los "
"anuncios en redes sociales apoyan a los anuncios de búsqueda)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:60016
#: c0b4573d3e2642ff8c6ef6c77b40c246
msgid ""
"Competitor Offers (I) and Market Growth (G) impact the marketing channels"
" and sales, which can confuse the understanding of cause and effect."
msgstr ""
"Las Ofertas de Competidores (I) y el Crecimiento del Mercado (G) impactan"
" los canales de marketing y las ventas, lo que puede confundir la "
"comprensión de causa y efecto."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:60018
#: bd711b6dba4e4ead9bde74ec24f6ef64
msgid ""
"We now need to define how these relationships work and create a model to "
"generate data that reflects these assumptions. This way, we can see how "
"well we can identify causal relationships using the data we gather."
msgstr ""
"Ahora necesitamos definir cómo funcionan estas relaciones y crear un "
"modelo para generar datos que reflejen estas suposiciones. De esta "
"manera, podemos ver qué tan bien podemos identificar relaciones causales "
"utilizando los datos que recopilamos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:80002
#: bc533902278249bda426b731f5aa66c1
msgid ""
"We set a date range between January 2022 and November 2024, at a daily "
"frequency."
msgstr ""
"Establecimos un rango de fechas entre enero de 2022 y noviembre de 2024, "
"con una frecuencia diaria."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:80004
#: 39f61a9e34664457a5dfbaf16438a187
msgid "Generating the Market Growth (Trend)"
msgstr "Generando el Crecimiento del Mercado (Tendencia)"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:80005
#: 941240172172453ebc64a83a6b82a450
msgid ""
"Next, we generate the data for **market growth**. We assume the market "
"growth follows a power-law trend, meaning that growth accelerates over "
"time rather than remaining constant. This can be mathematically defined "
"as:"
msgstr ""
"A continuación, generamos los datos para **el crecimiento del mercado**. "
"Asumimos que el crecimiento del mercado sigue una tendencia de ley de "
"potencias, lo que significa que el crecimiento se acelera con el tiempo "
"en lugar de permanecer constante. Esto se puede definir matemáticamente "
"como:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:80007
#: 7d247b2d8f8e4bb4bd3b33d90c7194a9
msgid ""
"\n"
"MG_{t} = (t + \\text{baseline})^{\\text{exponent}} - 1\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"MG_{t} = (t + \\text{baseline})^{\\text{exponent}} - 1\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:80011
#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:100012
#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:120010
#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:200012
#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560030
#: 00238927d37f4be686d074d27231754d 59e4c5b019ec4edda98fe8c60f355393
#: 644cb019df8b44acbf4b7128eba56d8e b837288593f24aa3b5d55c3e91c3119d
#: cbbf2d79b65f483eb484d776e5717a64
msgid "Where:"
msgstr "Dónde:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:80012
#: 7f729a1e60d9407185a2cc766be42b5f
msgid "$t$: The time index, representing days since the start of the date range."
msgstr ""
"$t$: El índice de tiempo, que representa los días desde el inicio del "
"rango de fechas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:80013
#: 5383dc392efd4fd2b6a5d3042c4a4596
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"$baseline$: A constant added to $t$ to shift the starting point of the "
"trend. This value affects the initial level of market growth. The "
"starting value of the function will be $(baseline)^{exponent} - 1$, not "
"0."
msgstr ""
"$baseline$: Una constante añadida a $t$ para desplazar el punto de inicio"
" de la tendencia. Este valor afecta el nivel inicial del crecimiento del "
"mercado. El valor inicial de la función será $(baseline)^{exponent} - 1$,"
" no 0."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:80014
#: 462b5a0ac0324266a36b1160975378a8
msgid ""
"$exponent$: The power to which the time index is raised, determining the "
"rate at which the trend accelerates over time."
msgstr ""
"$exponent$: La potencia a la que se eleva el índice de tiempo, "
"determinando la tasa a la que la tendencia se acelera con el tiempo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:100002
#: 2c337b9cac414ff28aff7f4a45fb171f
msgid "Generating the Holiday Effect"
msgstr "Generando el Efecto Vacacional"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:100004
#: 5a259bcb12b24a28800d3eab7afc14e7
msgid ""
"In this section, we simulate the effect of holidays on the market growth "
"trend. Certain holidays, like Christmas, can have a significant impact on"
" consumer behavior, leading to seasonal spikes in sales. To capture these"
" effects, we introduce a holiday signal based on Gaussian (normal) "
"distributions centered around specific holiday dates."
msgstr ""
"En esta sección, simulamos el efecto de las festividades en la tendencia "
"de crecimiento del mercado. Ciertas festividades, como la Navidad, pueden"
" tener un impacto significativo en el comportamiento del consumidor, lo "
"que lleva a picos estacionales en las ventas. Para capturar estos "
"efectos, introducimos una señal de festividad basada en distribuciones "
"gaussianas (normales) centradas en fechas específicas de festividades."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:100006
#: dec32566ebca4d239d50dbc0fe2eaad2
msgid "The function used to model the holiday effect is defined as follows:"
msgstr ""
"La función utilizada para modelar el efecto de las vacaciones se define "
"de la siguiente manera:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:100008
#: 38886be0048949568b651395709ff4b3
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"H_{t} = \\exp\\left(-0.5 \\left(\\frac{\\Delta "
"t}{\\sigma}\\right)^2\\right)\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"H_{t} = \\exp\\left(-0.5 \\left(\\frac{\\Delta t}{\\sigma}\\right)^2\\right)\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:100013
#: 413b4200b89d41df941eafc59513e934
msgid ""
"$\\Delta t$ is the time difference (in days) between the current date and"
" the holiday date."
msgstr ""
"$\\Delta t$ es la diferencia de tiempo (en días) entre la fecha actual y "
"la fecha de la festividad."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:100014
#: 2a434101aedf467e9547fc4b4db62a13
msgid ""
"$\\sigma$ is the standard deviation that controls the spread of the "
"effect around the holiday date."
msgstr ""
"$\\sigma$ es la desviación estándar que controla la dispersión del efecto"
" alrededor de la fecha de la festividad."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:100016
#: 47e21ad40a5c48fba4bf2b8fc30ce27c
msgid ""
"For each holiday, we calculate the holiday signal across the date range "
"and add a **holiday contribution** by scaling the signal with a holiday-"
"specific coefficient. This approach models seasonal holiday spikes using "
"Gaussian functions, which capture the transient increase in market "
"activity around holidays, and their respective decay over time."
msgstr ""
"Para cada festividad, calculamos la señal de la festividad a lo largo del"
" rango de fechas y añadimos una **contribución de festividad** escalando "
"la señal con un coeficiente específico de la festividad. Este enfoque "
"modela los picos estacionales de las festividades utilizando funciones "
"gaussianas, que capturan el aumento transitorio en la actividad del "
"mercado alrededor de las festividades y su respectivo decaimiento a lo "
"largo del tiempo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:120002
#: 656b2e27a8d347b0b11abf64c036889b
msgid "Modeling Competitor Offers"
msgstr "Modelando Ofertas de Competidores"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:120004
#: 948848d2a38343f99a771f7d57201390
msgid "To simulate the impact of competitor offers on market growth."
msgstr ""
"Para simular el impacto de las ofertas de los competidores en el "
"crecimiento del mercado."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:120006
#: 9ec0ab2fee8447138a286e34ec2ec6bc
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"C_{t} = -A \\cdot \\cos(\\omega \\cdot t) + C\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"C_{t} = -A \\cdot \\cos(\\omega \\cdot t) + C\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:120011
#: e53e5777bd324f499421d2d9689beca8
msgid ""
"$A$: The **amplitude** of the oscillation, representing the maximum "
"deviation from the center. In this context, it controls the intensity of "
"the competitor offers."
msgstr ""
"$A$: La **amplitud** de la oscilación, que representa la desviación "
"máxima del centro. En este contexto, controla la intensidad de las "
"ofertas de los competidores."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:120012
#: 8c67b5c4479444e3b3957de877381d3d
msgid ""
"$C$: The **center of oscillation**, setting the average level around "
"which competitor offers fluctuate."
msgstr ""
"$C$: El **centro de oscilación**, que establece el nivel promedio "
"alrededor del cual fluctúan las ofertas de los competidores."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:120013
#: 83f6d79e7cd049be8503a8fbb1020b2f
msgid ""
"$\\omega$: The **angular frequency**, which determines the frequency of "
"the oscillations. It’s calculated as: $\\omega = "
"\\frac{\\pi}{\\frac{n}{2}}$ where $n$ is the total number of data points."
" This ensures a complete cycle within the specified range."
msgstr ""
"$\\omega$: La **frecuencia angular**, que determina la frecuencia de las "
"oscilaciones. Se calcula como: $\\omega = \\frac{\\pi}{\\frac{n}{2}}$ "
"donde $n$ es el número total de puntos de datos. Esto asegura un ciclo "
"completo dentro del rango especificado."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:140002
#: cbaa255635434de688e56451543d0ef7
msgid ""
"With this form, we simulate a world where competitors offers increase "
"during the initial days of the year, and then decrease towards the end of"
" the year."
msgstr ""
"Con este formulario, simulamos un mundo donde las ofertas de los "
"competidores aumentan durante los primeros días del año y luego "
"disminuyen hacia el final del año."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:140004
#: e960448a3b664d6d9fb5509f9238690b
msgid "Modeling Marketing Channels"
msgstr "Modelando Canales de Marketing"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:140006
#: 41b8e8e2fa514429b9cea8482500bb5d
msgid ""
"In this section, we simulate two marketing channels, $x1$ and $x2$, which"
" represent different advertising channels (e.g., Search ads and Social "
"media campaigns). Each channel's behavior is influenced by random "
"variability and confounding effects from seasonal holidays and competitor"
" actions. Here’s how we model each channel mathematically:"
msgstr ""
"En esta sección, simulamos dos canales de marketing, $x1$ y $x2$, que "
"representan diferentes canales publicitarios (por ejemplo, anuncios de "
"búsqueda y campañas en redes sociales). El comportamiento de cada canal "
"está influenciado por la variabilidad aleatoria y los efectos confusos de"
" las festividades estacionales y las acciones de los competidores. Así es"
" como modelamos cada canal matemáticamente:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:140008
#: 2f17287c57954062be69306a649a7db3
msgid ""
"**Channel $x1$**: As mentioned before, we generate $x1$ which is affected"
" by the holiday signal, we could define it as:"
msgstr ""
"**Canal $x1$**: Como se mencionó anteriormente, generamos $x1$ que se ve "
"afectado por la señal de vacaciones, podríamos definirlo como:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:140011
#: f22d68a9a3da4b1ca90b83441cf5ab06
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"I_{x1_t} = S_{x1_t} + H_{t} \\times \\alpha_{x1}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"I_{x1_t} = S_{x1_t} + H_{t} \\times \\alpha_{x1}\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:140015
#: 3a103838e645408bb40b97222773f87c
msgid ""
"**Channel $x2$**: On the other hand, we generate $x2$ which is affected "
"by the holiday signal, the influence of $x1$ and the competitor offers. "
"We could define it as:"
msgstr ""
"**Canal $x2$**: Por otro lado, generamos $x2$ que se ve afectado por la "
"señal de vacaciones, la influencia de $x1$ y las ofertas de los "
"competidores. Podríamos definirlo como:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:140018
#: 1304d19848444eae897812556e40aae0
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"I_{x2_t} = S_{x2_t} + H_{t} \\times \\alpha_{x2} + (I_{x1_t} \\times "
"\\alpha_{x1_x2}) + (C_{t} \\times \\alpha_{x2})\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"I_{x2_t} = S_{x2_t} + H_{t} \\times \\alpha_{x2} + (I_{x1_t} \\times \\alpha_{x1_x2}) + (C_{t} \\times \\alpha_{x2})\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:140022
#: 4956220bd2a9488490fb2d6b17e41b45
msgid "Interpretation"
msgstr "Interpretación"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:140024
#: 65e08f3b543f4e53b4756c2513e96c52
msgid ""
"These equations allow us to capture the complex dynamics influencing each"
" marketing channel:"
msgstr ""
"Estas ecuaciones nos permiten capturar la dinámica compleja que influye "
"en cada canal de marketing:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:140025
#: 4a144c63fa244ef1b5a5c75998865d35
msgid ""
"**Holiday Effects** increase channel activity around specific dates, "
"simulating seasonal spikes."
msgstr ""
"**Efectos de Vacaciones** aumentan la actividad del canal alrededor de "
"fechas específicas, simulando picos estacionales."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:140026
#: 4512ed4db6e4478ca0ceb402b88bf128
msgid ""
"**Cross-channel Influences** introduce interdependencies, modeling how "
"one channel's success can amplify another’s."
msgstr ""
"**Influencias entre canales** introducen interdependencias, modelando "
"cómo el éxito de un canal puede amplificar el de otro."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:140027
#: 6b3308446fd44d7c944a1c9c59520e0f
msgid ""
"**Competitor Effects** introduce fluctuations due to external factors, "
"showing how competitive pressure can decrease engagement or "
"effectiveness."
msgstr ""
"**Efectos de la competencia** introducen fluctuaciones debido a factores "
"externos, mostrando cómo la presión competitiva puede disminuir el "
"compromiso o la efectividad."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:140029
#: abc84d96fe0d44de8e1ab19c7da549ac
msgid ""
"This approach reflects real-world conditions, where marketing channels "
"are not isolated but affected by seasonal trends, competitor actions, and"
" synergies across different channels."
msgstr ""
"Este enfoque refleja las condiciones del mundo real, donde los canales de"
" marketing no están aislados, sino que se ven afectados por tendencias "
"estacionales, acciones de los competidores y sinergias entre diferentes "
"canales."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:170002
#: 184715fde10a409b812670e1114b24d2
msgid ""
"The two generated signals wil represent the \"impressions\" of the two "
"marketing channels. Basically, we are simulating the exposure that we "
"would observe from a media platform, reported after we run a campaign."
msgstr ""
"Las dos señales generadas representarán las \"impresiones\" de los dos "
"canales de marketing. Básicamente, estamos simulando la exposición que "
"observaríamos de una plataforma de medios, reportada después de ejecutar "
"una campaña."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:170004
#: fbb60e4d96334dad9cc326849b2c8b0c
msgid ""
"The level of exposure doesn't impact our sales in a linear way, so we "
"need to apply a transformation to account for that. We'll use a geometric"
" adstock transformation, which is a common technique in marketing mix "
"modeling to account for the adstock/lagging effect, and a michaelis-"
"menten saturation to account for the diminishing returns effect."
msgstr ""
"El nivel de exposición no impacta nuestras ventas de manera lineal, por "
"lo que necesitamos aplicar una transformación para tenerlo en cuenta. "
"Utilizaremos una transformación de adstock geométrico, que es una técnica"
" común en la modelización de mezcla de marketing para considerar el "
"efecto de adstock/retraso, y una saturación de michaelis-menten para "
"tener en cuenta el efecto de rendimientos decrecientes."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:170006
#: 3fa64aec27b844019c06690e44df66d0
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Similar as the {ref}`mmm_example`."
msgstr "De manera similar a {ref}`mmm_example`."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:200002
#: 5e0878fe4643468ab5d6fa71396053ac
msgid "Defining the Sales (Target)"
msgstr "Definiendo las Ventas (Objetivo)"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:200004
#: 94d1c62d03f847218bf2fb576f9ff915
msgid ""
"Finally, we define the sales or revenue (target) variable, which is "
"affected by the market growth, the competitor offers, the holiday "
"contributions, the saturated media costs and a noise term."
msgstr ""
"Finalmente, definimos la variable de ventas o ingresos (objetivo), que se"
" ve afectada por el crecimiento del mercado, las ofertas de los "
"competidores, las contribuciones de las festividades, los costos de "
"medios saturados y un término de ruido."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:200006
#: 3fac3712ef4a4a22b29855d83687ba73
msgid "The variable, $y$, is defined as follows:"
msgstr "La variable, $y$, se define de la siguiente manera:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:200008
#: fdb9a237e956484d812e311bf7225cd7
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"y_{t} = Intercept + f(MG_{t}) - f(C_{t}) + f(H_{t}) + m(I_{x1_t}) + "
"m(I_{x2_t}) + \\epsilon\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"y_{t} = Intercept + f(MG_{t}) - f(C_{t}) + f(H_{t}) + m(I_{x1_t}) + m(I_{x2_t}) + \\epsilon\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:200013
#: 6be2cdc61bf2444a8c680d976fcd7e73
msgid ""
"**Intercept**: A baseline level of sales, set to 1.5, representing the "
"base sales level in the absence of other effects."
msgstr ""
"**Intercepto**: Un nivel base de ventas, establecido en 1.5, que "
"representa el nivel base de ventas en ausencia de otros efectos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:200014
#: bdefa977a15844238a2e7fab51e80114
msgid ""
"**Market Growth**: Represents the underlying trend in sales due to long-"
"term growth, with an implicit coefficient of 1, adding a steady upward "
"influence."
msgstr ""
"**Crecimiento del Mercado**: Representa la tendencia subyacente en las "
"ventas debido al crecimiento a largo plazo, con un coeficiente implícito "
"de 1, añadiendo una influencia ascendente constante."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:200015
#: 0533fe2a626146a08c8b97a9cd0647e4
msgid ""
"**Competitor Offers**: Directly reduces sales, with an implicit "
"coefficient of -1, simulating the negative impact of competitor actions "
"on the target variable."
msgstr ""
"**Ofertas de Competidores**: Reduce directamente las ventas, con un "
"coeficiente implícito de -1, simulando el impacto negativo de las "
"acciones de los competidores en la variable objetivo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:200016
#: b5ee3de054c3423bafb8a3f82d3bf700
msgid ""
"**Holiday Contributions**: Adds sales spikes around holiday periods, "
"capturing the seasonal increase in consumer demand."
msgstr ""
"**Contribuciones Festivas**: Añade picos de ventas durante los períodos "
"festivos, capturando el aumento estacional en la demanda del consumidor."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:200017
#: b05b5dbf4b5b4edab6f849aa635dc6a9
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**$m(Impressions_{x1_t})$ and $m(Impressions_{x2_t})$**: Represent the "
"**saturated adstock** values for the marketing channels $x1$ and $x2$."
msgstr ""
"**$m(Impressions_{x1_t})$ y $m(Impressions_{x2_t})$**: Representan los "
"valores de **adstock saturado** para los canales de marketing $x1$ y "
"$x2$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:200018
#: 982e77ade80a450791cf90b393192efb
msgid ""
"**Noise $\\epsilon$**: A small random error term, drawn from a normal "
"distribution with mean 0 and standard deviation 0.08, to account for "
"unexplained variability in sales."
msgstr ""
"**Ruido $\\epsilon$**: Un pequeño término de error aleatorio, extraído de"
" una distribución normal con media 0 y desviación estándar 0.08, para "
"tener en cuenta la variabilidad no explicada en las ventas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:230002
#: 9efc1dc3b8b54e14a7d5e35d176360d3
msgid "Let’s recap what we’ve done so far:"
msgstr "Hagamos un resumen de lo que hemos hecho hasta ahora:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:230004
#: 27ba5184814142468ec324b9c165ef52
msgid ""
"We created a hypothesis about how things in the world interact and how "
"those interactions are connected."
msgstr ""
"Creamos una hipótesis sobre cómo interactúan las cosas en el mundo y cómo"
" están conectadas esas interacciones."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:230005
#: 01c8de5ea000481b912523c877ce30df
msgid ""
"We turned our hypothesis into a mathematical model that reflects these "
"connections."
msgstr ""
"Convertimos nuestra hipótesis en un modelo matemático que refleja estas "
"conexiones."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:230006
#: 0386f5f71df24339983c11ecf242d1a0
msgid "We generated data that fits with our hypothesis."
msgstr "Generamos datos que se ajustan a nuestra hipótesis."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:230007
#: 4a5b4ee3d8a1468891effd1c823c0415
msgid "Now we are ready to find the model that best explains our data."
msgstr ""
"Ahora estamos listos para encontrar el modelo que mejor explique nuestros"
" datos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:230009
#: 8264d87b51054cdbb3216650185d9c39
msgid ""
"In Bayesian terms, we call this the data generating process, which "
"corresponds to the structural causal model in causal terms."
msgstr ""
"En términos bayesianos, llamamos a esto el proceso generador de datos, "
"que corresponde al modelo causal estructural en términos causales."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:230011
#: 9b15c693b9d94efa8fa31f764a697d56
msgid ""
"All models we write in PyMC are structural causal models. Even if we "
"don’t aim for a causal interpretation, our model still seeks to explain a"
" specific data generating process."
msgstr ""
"Todos los modelos que escribimos en PyMC son modelos causales "
"estructurales. Incluso si no buscamos una interpretación causal, nuestro "
"modelo aún busca explicar un proceso específico de generación de datos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:230013
#: 96923bbf5063416b8e4c7e0d02ff3534
msgid ""
"Recognizing this is crucial because it shapes our decisions when building"
" the model and choosing which variables to include. After our previous "
"work, we should have a good idea of which variables are most important in"
" explaining sales. However, if we forget what we discussed earlier, we "
"won't know how to start building the model."
msgstr ""
"Reconocer esto es crucial porque influye en nuestras decisiones al "
"construir el modelo y elegir qué variables incluir. Después de nuestro "
"trabajo anterior, deberíamos tener una buena idea de cuáles son las "
"variables más importantes para explicar las ventas. Sin embargo, si "
"olvidamos lo que discutimos anteriormente, no sabremos cómo empezar a "
"construir el modelo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:230015
#: 1e092560028f4709a1694763135807f7
msgid "The Real Challenge"
msgstr "El verdadero desafío"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:230017
#: 19429b55a65044aa8107054e41bf7531
msgid ""
"In real life, we don't know the actual data generating process; we only "
"have observed data. Often, we receive a dataset like the one shown below."
msgstr ""
"En la vida real, no conocemos el proceso real que genera los datos; solo "
"tenemos datos observados. A menudo, recibimos un conjunto de datos como "
"el que se muestra a continuación."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:250002
#: fb4636a873994375829a72f9fca52f12
msgid ""
"If we have PyMC installed, the simplest approach would be to include all "
"our variables in a model and run it. This is like using any model "
"available on the market, checking correlations, and selecting the most "
"relevant variables. This method essentially means, “Let’s control for "
"everything that might relate to sales.”"
msgstr ""
"Si tenemos PyMC instalado, el enfoque más simple sería incluir todas "
"nuestras variables en un modelo y ejecutarlo. Esto es similar a utilizar "
"cualquier modelo disponible en el mercado, verificando correlaciones y "
"seleccionando las variables más relevantes. Este método significa "
"esencialmente: \"Controlaremos todo lo que pueda relacionarse con las "
"ventas.\""

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:250004
#: 88082f02a1c34a5385bfb488bb37e74d
msgid ""
"Note: This approach is not bad, but it misses using valuable information "
"and prior knowledge about the business and its inner relationships."
msgstr ""
"Nota: Este enfoque no es malo, pero no utiliza información valiosa y "
"conocimientos previos sobre el negocio y sus relaciones internas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:250006
#: b419e6ed0cf8460aa7d429fb8d2d984b
msgid ""
"We can separate the target variable from the potential factors that "
"influence it. Then, we can begin training our initial correlation-based "
"model."
msgstr ""
"Podemos separar la variable objetivo de los factores potenciales que la "
"influyen. Luego, podemos comenzar a entrenar nuestro modelo inicial "
"basado en correlaciones."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:290002
#: dec2866655814b4c975dbbe32721f82c
msgid ""
"With the small lines of code above, our media mix model is set up, and we"
" can now start training it."
msgstr ""
"Con las pequeñas líneas de código anteriores, nuestro modelo de mezcla de"
" medios está configurado y ahora podemos comenzar a entrenarlo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:310002
#: 79599af758d448b0b20345ff94126f22
msgid ""
"Since PyMC is structural, we can show our model as a directed acyclic "
"graph (DAG). This graph helps us see how the parameters and variables "
"relate to each other and understand our decisions in the modeling "
"process."
msgstr ""
"Dado que PyMC es estructural, podemos representar nuestro modelo como un "
"grafo acíclico dirigido (DAG). Este grafo nos ayuda a ver cómo se "
"relacionan los parámetros y las variables entre sí y a comprender "
"nuestras decisiones en el proceso de modelado."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:310004
#: bc7fb1d3918f4bd3bf8695a4e7a3f7be
msgid ""
"We can use the `model_to_graphviz` function to create this visual "
"representation."
msgstr ""
"Podemos utilizar la función `model_to_graphviz` para crear esta "
"representación visual."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:330002
#: 5e85de15673f417c8d49a0556a72c90b
msgid ""
"Our DAG is quite simple. It includes our channels, which have two "
"dimensions: date and channel. It also has an intercept variable that "
"captures baseline sales or revenue, which are factors outside of our "
"control, and a term to reflect random variance."
msgstr ""
"Nuestro DAG es bastante simple. Incluye nuestros canales, que tienen dos "
"dimensiones: fecha y canal. También tiene una variable de intercepción "
"que captura las ventas o ingresos base, que son factores fuera de nuestro"
" control, y un término para reflejar la variación aleatoria."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:330004
#: e69d3f4d27394a278a0ffcee968414f1
msgid ""
"In simpler terms, we can express the underlying function of this media "
"mix model as:"
msgstr ""
"En términos más simples, podemos expresar la función subyacente de este "
"modelo de mezcla de medios como:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:330006
#: d6b1c2df4a61424a9246270a824337d6
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mu & = \\beta_0 \\cdot \\text{baseline} +\n"
" m(\\text{x1}, \\theta_{\\text{x1}}) +\n"
" m(\\text{x2}, \\theta_{\\text{x2}})\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mu & = \\beta_0 \\cdot \\text{baseline} +\n"
" m(\\text{x1}, \\theta_{\\text{x1}}) +\n"
" m(\\text{x2}, \\theta_{\\text{x2}})\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:330014
#: d40486880bfc4564891633ff811c31c2
msgid "Here:"
msgstr "Aquí:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:330015
#: 521691fc8f324fd2bd2002707b001ab1
msgid ""
"$\\mu$ represents the predicted outcome variable (like sales or revenue) "
"based on the combined effects of our input variables."
msgstr ""
"$\\mu$ representa la variable de resultado predicha (como ventas o "
"ingresos) basada en los efectos combinados de nuestras variables de "
"entrada."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:330016
#: 73dba1572f1541e297cc0b3631199398
msgid "$\\beta_0$ is the coefficient for the baseline variable."
msgstr "$\\beta_0$ es el coeficiente para la variable base."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:330017
#: 00b1b778f34b4399b77d7292391ed368
msgid ""
"$m(\\text{x1}, \\theta_{\\text{x1}})$ and $m(\\text{x2}, "
"\\theta_{\\text{x2}})$ are non-linear transformations of $x1$ and $x2$ "
"that capture their varying impacts."
msgstr ""
"$m(\\text{x1}, \\theta_{\\text{x1}})$ y $m(\\text{x2}, "
"\\theta_{\\text{x2}})$ son transformaciones no lineales de $x1$ y $x2$ "
"que capturan sus impactos variables."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:330019
#: ee94bd50cb9b4ef2be152cfd7c181efe
msgid ""
"Based on this, we think this function will help us understand the impact "
"of $x1$ and $x2$. Thus, we can outline the causal DAG we believe is "
"correct."
msgstr ""
"Basado en esto, creemos que esta función nos ayudará a entender el "
"impacto de $x1$ y $x2$. Así, podemos esbozar el DAG causal que creemos "
"que es correcto."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:350002
#: eaaac64bceaf41f0a8de793872d304d5
msgid "How can we infer this DAG from our current model?"
msgstr "¿Cómo podemos inferir este DAG de nuestro modelo actual?"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:350004
#: c782602e3cd248f18104463973959d49
msgid ""
"During the development of our model, we established a specific structure "
"and flow for our data. We concluded that the impacts of our channels "
"operate independently of each other. Moreover, we determined that if any "
"component of our ecosystem is missing, its influence will be accounted "
"for by the baseline term due to this equation. As you can see, even by "
"adopting this basic model, we are making significant assumptions."
msgstr ""
"Durante el desarrollo de nuestro modelo, establecimos una estructura y un"
" flujo específicos para nuestros datos. Concluimos que los impactos de "
"nuestros canales operan de manera independiente entre sí. Además, "
"determinamos que si falta algún componente de nuestro ecosistema, su "
"influencia será contabilizada por el término base debido a esta ecuación."
" Como puede ver, incluso al adoptar este modelo básico, estamos haciendo "
"suposiciones significativas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:350006
#: 79f964daa04a44b28002a2790e197560
msgid ""
"On one hand, you are assuming that the impact is not linear by applying "
"these transformations, and you are suggesting that the impact is positive"
" and that there may be a maximum delay of a certain number of days."
msgstr ""
"Por un lado, usted está asumiendo que el impacto no es lineal al aplicar "
"estas transformaciones, y está sugiriendo que el impacto es positivo y "
"que puede haber un retraso máximo de un cierto número de días."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:350008
#: fdc7e34698404e1998cb211fecaa8700
msgid ""
"You've even defined the direction of your relationships. By defining "
"these relationships and assuming no direct causal connections between our"
" variables, we can conclude that, if the nature of their relationship is "
"accurately represented by the provided equation, then by controlling the "
"relevant channels, we could uncover their true effects."
msgstr ""
"Incluso has definido la dirección de tus relaciones. Al definir estas "
"relaciones y asumir que no hay conexiones causales directas entre "
"nuestras variables, podemos concluir que, si la naturaleza de su relación"
" está representada con precisión por la ecuación proporcionada, entonces "
"al controlar los canales relevantes, podríamos descubrir sus verdaderos "
"efectos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:350010
#: f7895314f10c4dfa9275efdc34a0a797
msgid ""
"This leads us to which causal DAG we assume is correct, based on our "
"previous assumptions. If you recognize this process, congratulations! "
"You've created a generative model or Structural Causal Model, with a "
"Structural Causal Equation, using PyMC-marketing."
msgstr ""
"Esto nos lleva a cuál DAG causal asumimos que es correcto, basado en "
"nuestras suposiciones anteriores. Si reconoces este proceso, "
"¡felicitaciones! Has creado un modelo generativo o Modelo Causal "
"Estructural, con una Ecuación Causal Estructural, utilizando PyMC-"
"marketing."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:350012
#: 2df3208314d84dd4bbf9ff6b4b497e4b
msgid ""
"Note: As you can see, based on our assumptions and the variables we "
"included, we can backtrack and infer the causal DAG we are inherently "
"assuming. This backtracking process can be using and formalize on causal "
"discovery algorithms to automatically infer the several causal DAGs based"
" on how our regression model and their estimates respond to the data."
msgstr ""
"Nota: Como puede ver, basándonos en nuestras suposiciones y las variables"
" que incluimos, podemos retroceder e inferir el DAG causal que estamos "
"asumiendo inherentemente. Este proceso de retroceso puede ser utilizado y"
" formalizado en algoritmos de descubrimiento causal para inferir "
"automáticamente los varios DAG causales en función de cómo nuestro modelo"
" de regresión y sus estimaciones responden a los datos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:350014
#: 70f831e5ab2b40618a6442c8a7d81eeb
msgid ""
"However, this Causal DAG does not depict the true Causal DAG. Since our "
"PyMC model is structural and causal, we must ask: *What happens if I "
"create a model with a different causal structure than the real one?*"
msgstr ""
"Sin embargo, este DAG causal no representa el verdadero DAG causal. Dado "
"que nuestro modelo PyMC es estructural y causal, debemos preguntar: *¿Qué"
" sucede si creo un modelo con una estructura causal diferente a la real?*"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:360002
#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:620002
#: 8467e56d1f124f61b370d1d2378fca8f 9301b0e585b74218b7039e9c0a275f97
msgid "\\displaystyle 0"
msgstr "\\displaystyle 0"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:370002
#: 9b26adfbe2064c62997033a8fd18bb56
msgid ""
"Because all PyMC models are generative models, they are able to \"talk\" "
"about the causal relationships that are present in the data generating "
"process. If we have a model that is not consistent with the true causal "
"relationships, the model will fail during the exploration of the "
"parameter space."
msgstr ""
"Porque todos los modelos de PyMC son modelos generativos, son capaces de "
"\"hablar\" sobre las relaciones causales que están presentes en el "
"proceso de generación de datos. Si tenemos un modelo que no es "
"consistente con las verdaderas relaciones causales, el modelo fallará "
"durante la exploración del espacio de parámetros."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:370004
#: 20d9f7936ecf465393e5f4d502684854
msgid ""
"For example, if you assume that variable  A  causes variable  B  (i.e.,  "
"A -> B ), but in reality,  B  causes  A  or they are confounded by an "
"unobserved variable, your model’s structure misrepresents the actual "
"relationships. This misalignment creates inconsistencies between the "
"model and the data, resulting in a posterior distribution that is "
"challenging for the sampler to explore. The posterior may exhibit "
"pathological features such as multimodality, strong correlations between "
"parameters, or regions of high curvature."
msgstr ""
"Por ejemplo, si asume que la variable A causa la variable B (es decir, A "
"-> B), pero en realidad, B causa A o están confundidas por una variable "
"no observada, la estructura de su modelo representa incorrectamente las "
"relaciones reales. Este desajuste crea inconsistencias entre el modelo y "
"los datos, lo que resulta en una distribución posterior que es difícil de"
" explorar para el muestreador. La posterior puede exhibir características"
" patológicas como multimodalidad, fuertes correlaciones entre parámetros "
"o regiones de alta curvatura."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:370006
#: 4ca83e7171c54e21953d4a062bb894d5
msgid ""
"A model like this will get divergencies, because these occur when the "
"numerical integrator used in Hamiltonian Monte Carlo (HMC) cannot "
"accurately simulate the trajectory through the parameter space, often due"
" to steep gradients or discontinuities in the posterior. If you think "
"about it, incorrect causal assumptions may force the sampler into "
"incompatible regions of the parameter space, causing the numerical "
"integration to fail."
msgstr ""
"Un modelo como este presentará divergencias, porque estas ocurren cuando "
"el integrador numérico utilizado en el muestreo de Monte Carlo "
"Hamiltoniano (HMC) no puede simular con precisión la trayectoria a través"
" del espacio de parámetros, a menudo debido a gradientes pronunciados o "
"discontinuidades en el posterior. Si lo piensas, suposiciones causales "
"incorrectas pueden forzar al muestreador a entrar en regiones "
"incompatibles del espacio de parámetros, lo que provoca que la "
"integración numérica falle."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:370008
#: 1756e4394cc94f28b3940ddfc372e216
msgid ""
"When we evaluate time series generative models, particulary bayesian "
"models, we should always evaluate models with additional metrics on top "
"of the pure fit metrics, such as divergences, rhat, ess, etc."
msgstr ""
"Cuando evaluamos modelos generativos de series temporales, "
"particularmente modelos bayesianos, siempre debemos evaluar los modelos "
"con métricas adicionales además de las métricas de ajuste puro, como "
"divergencias, rhat, ess, etc."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:370011
#: 53bd95d6f4e748b491ff51c6e279ce6a
msgid "Lets observe the fit of our current model 👀"
msgstr "Observemos el ajuste de nuestro modelo actual 👀"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:390002
#: b87a6499928b427bae354669a5d4860a
msgid ""
"Great, our model looks amazing! At first glance, our model evaluation "
"appears quite satisfactory. The $R^2$ value is decent, and the "
"uncertainty in the credible intervals is manageable."
msgstr ""
"Genial, ¡nuestro modelo se ve increíble! A primera vista, la evaluación "
"de nuestro modelo parece bastante satisfactoria. El valor de $R^2$ es "
"decente y la incertidumbre en los intervalos creíbles es manejable."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:390004
#: 5b544563562f40288adaf3baf3039078
msgid ""
"However, the pressing question remains: are we truly capturing the "
"underlying causal signals?"
msgstr ""
"Sin embargo, la pregunta apremiante sigue siendo: ¿estamos realmente "
"capturando las señales causales subyacentes?"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:410002
#: e5ea9509978c4b35b75b81502a7b3185
msgid ""
"Our model struggles to accurately capture the true causal effect of media"
" variables, suggesting it may be misspecified."
msgstr ""
"Nuestro modelo tiene dificultades para capturar con precisión el "
"verdadero efecto causal de las variables mediáticas, lo que sugiere que "
"puede estar mal especificado."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:410004
#: 96c2e6c4ee4f4fae8c2ffbe6ac750c08
msgid ""
"In this context, although we can use the true model to compare the actual"
" effects with the model's recovered effects, real-life situations often "
"lack this clarity. Therefore, we need methods to identify and compare the"
" recovered effects with the true ones."
msgstr ""
"En este contexto, aunque podemos utilizar el modelo verdadero para "
"comparar los efectos reales con los efectos recuperados del modelo, las "
"situaciones de la vida real a menudo carecen de esta claridad. Por lo "
"tanto, necesitamos métodos para identificar y comparar los efectos "
"recuperados con los verdaderos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:410006
#: 01714d2da5684366a52b330360062520
msgid ""
"This is where **CausalPy** is useful. It enables the creation of quasi-"
"experiments to determine the causal impact of media variables, allowing "
"for comparison between our model's results and those from these "
"experiments. You can learn more about [CausalPy "
"here](https://causalpy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/)."
msgstr ""
"Este es el lugar donde **CausalPy** resulta útil. Permite la creación de "
"cuasi-experimentos para determinar el impacto causal de las variables "
"mediáticas, lo que permite la comparación entre los resultados de nuestro"
" modelo y los de estos experimentos. Puede aprender más sobre [CausalPy "
"aquí](https://causalpy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:410008
#: 5e49f6d2592b443bb48f4cb1a1521335
msgid "Utilizing Causal Identification"
msgstr "Utilizando la Identificación Causal"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:410009
#: 9fdfcc05d4104feba9ca25fca8ca6ac1
msgid ""
"Instead of randomly adding variables to our regression, we should use a "
"causal framework to build our model. A language which help us to "
"translate our ideas and hypothesis into a graphical representation which "
"we can interrogate. Doing so, we can understant if we are overlooking an "
"important variable."
msgstr ""
"En lugar de agregar variables al azar a nuestra regresión, deberíamos "
"utilizar un marco causal para construir nuestro modelo. Un lenguaje que "
"nos ayude a traducir nuestras ideas e hipótesis en una representación "
"gráfica que podamos interrogar. Al hacerlo, podemos entender si estamos "
"pasando por alto una variable importante."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:440002
#: 6be95e1576574d6cb7607c57f20f13b4
msgid ""
"We’ve added a new column called `outcome_node` for our target variable "
"and defined the `dag` parameter as a representation of the causal "
"Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG). We included `holiday_signal` as a control "
"variable in our model because it significantly influences the target "
"variable and may have been missed before. After ran that, we received a "
"warning that channel columns are being treated as default treatment "
"variables, indicating they are our focus for estimating the true causal "
"impact (default behavior)."
msgstr ""
"Hemos añadido una nueva columna llamada `outcome_node` para nuestra "
"variable objetivo y definido el parámetro `dag` como una representación "
"del Grafo Acíclico Dirigido (DAG) causal. Incluimos `holiday_signal` como"
" una variable de control en nuestro modelo porque influye "
"significativamente en la variable objetivo y puede haber sido pasada por "
"alto anteriormente. Después de ejecutar eso, recibimos una advertencia de"
" que las columnas de canal se están tratando como variables de "
"tratamiento por defecto, lo que indica que son nuestro enfoque para "
"estimar el verdadero impacto causal (comportamiento por defecto)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:440004
#: 5e465476d71e4f66a39a855e023274d8
msgid ""
"Now, we can examine the adjustment set of variables needed to reveal the "
"true causal effect of our treatment variables."
msgstr ""
"Ahora, podemos examinar el conjunto de variables de ajuste necesarias "
"para revelar el verdadero efecto causal de nuestras variables de "
"tratamiento."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:460002
#: d60ba3da0e56427b959e3fcbfe1f43aa
msgid ""
"Great, we got a new piece of important information. We are missing the "
"`holiday_signal` variable in the adjustment set, meaning, to find the "
"true causal effect of `x1` and `x2`, we don’t need to control for "
"`holiday_signal`. So, why we could not recover the true causal effect of "
"`x1` and `x2` before? Perhaps the specified DAG was not true, meaning its"
" possible that the relationship between `x1` and `x2` is confounded by "
"the `holiday_signal` variable?"
msgstr ""
"Excelente, hemos obtenido una nueva pieza de información importante. Nos "
"falta la variable `holiday_signal` en el conjunto de ajustes, lo que "
"significa que, para encontrar el verdadero efecto causal de `x1` y `x2`, "
"no necesitamos controlar por `holiday_signal`. Entonces, ¿por qué no "
"pudimos recuperar el verdadero efecto causal de `x1` y `x2` antes? Quizás"
" el DAG especificado no era verdadero, lo que significa que es posible "
"que la relación entre `x1` y `x2` esté confundida por la variable "
"`holiday_signal`?"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:460004
#: 7834254095cb446bb667edc1556aa9fd
msgid "Lets see if this is the case."
msgstr "Veamos si este es el caso."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:480002
#: 4fff7da640454a06bc86373d045fe02f
msgid ""
"Now, with a new adjustment set, we see that if we do not control for "
"`holiday_signal`, we cannot identify the true causal effect of `x1` and "
"`x2` since they are influenced by this variable. This looks more close to"
" what happened before, after compare the true contribution of `x1` and "
"`x2` with the recovered contribution."
msgstr ""
"Ahora, con un nuevo conjunto de ajustes, vemos que si no controlamos por "
"`holiday_signal`, no podemos identificar el verdadero efecto causal de "
"`x1` y `x2`, ya que están influenciados por esta variable. Esto se "
"asemeja más a lo que ocurrió antes, después de comparar la verdadera "
"contribución de `x1` y `x2` con la contribución recuperada."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:480004
#: 1422458f027d4b2c88287e689f4b2df9
msgid ""
"Note: We define this adjustment set using the `CausalGraphModel` class. "
"We rely on `dowhy` to help us identify the adjustment set. You can learn "
"more about `dowhy` [here](https://www.pywhy.org/dowhy/v0.9.1/)."
msgstr ""
"Nota: Definimos este conjunto de ajuste utilizando la clase "
"`CausalGraphModel`. Dependemos de `dowhy` para ayudarnos a identificar el"
" conjunto de ajuste. Puede aprender más sobre `dowhy` "
"[aquí](https://www.pywhy.org/dowhy/v0.9.1/)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:480006
#: 283c0394a57d4088b9e946848476d668
msgid ""
"We use the `backdoor` criterion to choose the adjustment set. This means "
"we look for variables that, when we control for them, block all the "
"backdoor paths between `x1` and `x2`. These paths can create false links "
"between the treatment and outcome variables. If we don’t address these "
"paths, our causal estimates may be off. To understand the causal effect "
"accurately, we need to block these paths by adjusting for the confounding"
" variables. You can read more about the backdoor criterion in Aleksander "
"Molak's book [here](https://www.amazon.com/Causal-Inference-Discovery-"
"Python-learning/dp/1804612987)."
msgstr ""
"Utilizamos el criterio `backdoor` para elegir el conjunto de ajuste. Esto"
" significa que buscamos variables que, al controlarlas, bloquean todos "
"los caminos de retroceso entre `x1` y `x2`. Estos caminos pueden crear "
"vínculos falsos entre las variables de tratamiento y resultado. Si no "
"abordamos estos caminos, nuestras estimaciones causales pueden estar "
"equivocadas. Para entender el efecto causal con precisión, necesitamos "
"bloquear estos caminos ajustando las variables de confusión. Puede leer "
"más sobre el criterio backdoor en el libro de Aleksander Molak "
"[aquí](https://www.amazon.com/Causal-Inference-Discovery-Python-"
"learning/dp/1804612987)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:480008
#: 36ceb9c2a5ea48f7816bb4fc77e639e6
msgid ""
"Now, let’s say we create a new variable called `holiday_signal` to "
"control for the holiday effect. Adding this variable to our dataset "
"should help us find the true causal effect of `x1` and `x2`, right?"
msgstr ""
"Ahora, digamos que creamos una nueva variable llamada `holiday_signal` "
"para controlar el efecto de las festividades. Agregar esta variable a "
"nuestro conjunto de datos debería ayudarnos a encontrar el verdadero "
"efecto causal de `x1` y `x2`, ¿verdad?"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:520002
#: 707011d4debf4e459f3149929aaf319e
msgid ""
"We got even more divergencies 🤪, whats happening here? Everything is "
"worse? Even if we added a new variable to control for the "
"`holiday_signal`? This looks weird, because we are adding a variable that"
" should help us to identify the true causal effect of `x1` and `x2`."
msgstr ""
"Tenemos aún más divergencias 🤪, ¿qué está sucediendo aquí? ¿Todo está "
"peor? ¿Incluso si añadimos una nueva variable para controlar el "
"`holiday_signal`? Esto se ve extraño, porque estamos añadiendo una "
"variable que debería ayudarnos a identificar el verdadero efecto causal "
"de `x1` y `x2`."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:520004
#: f69af150e719431d8ee24a63dbd70d46
msgid "Lets see the fit of our model 👀"
msgstr "Veamos el ajuste de nuestro modelo 👀"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:540002
#: b2fa678e93d241379cdf0755b1178305
msgid ""
"Somehow $R^2$ is the same as before, even though the credible intervals "
"blow up around the holiday peaks. Could this be a good signal? Maybe we "
"are recovering the true causal effect of `x1` and `x2`?"
msgstr ""
"De alguna manera, $R^2$ es el mismo que antes, aunque los intervalos "
"creíbles se disparan alrededor de los picos de las festividades. ¿Podría ser"
" esto una buena señal? ¿Quizás estamos recuperando el verdadero efecto "
"causal de `x1` y `x2`?"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560002
#: b3598fbb963e40b697b41c30413ca20a
msgid ""
"At this point, we might feel like we have lost everything. It may seem "
"that some kind of bad luck is affecting our data. Or, we could have an "
"unknown factor that is influencing our marketing results without our "
"notice."
msgstr ""
"En este punto, podríamos sentir que hemos perdido todo. Puede parecer que"
" algún tipo de mala suerte está afectando nuestros datos. O, podríamos "
"tener un factor desconocido que está influyendo en nuestros resultados de"
" marketing sin que nos demos cuenta."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560004
#: a0bc216862d64b9fb4fa2b70cfab685b
msgid ""
"After some reflection, we can consider that our competitors’ actions, "
"like their offers and discounts, could be impacting our marketing "
"results. In other words, when our competitors spend more on marketing, "
"they can take away some of our potential incremental sales. Even if we "
"spend the same amount to get exposure, aggressive competitor offers can "
"pull customers away from us as they buy other products instead."
msgstr ""
"Después de una reflexión, podemos considerar que las acciones de nuestros"
" competidores, como sus ofertas y descuentos, podrían estar impactando "
"nuestros resultados de marketing. En otras palabras, cuando nuestros "
"competidores gastan más en marketing, pueden llevarse algunas de nuestras"
" posibles ventas incrementales. Incluso si gastamos la misma cantidad "
"para obtener exposición, las ofertas agresivas de los competidores pueden"
" desviar a los clientes de nosotros mientras compran otros productos en "
"su lugar."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560006
#: 1d02e4ca7ebb4da0805a86dc3fe5ed11
msgid ""
"Will this affect all our channels the same way? Probably not. Our "
"competitors may not impact our brand awareness, but they likely influence"
" our customers’ consideration. We might think that $x2$ is more affected "
"by our competitors than $x1$. This is because $x2$ is closer to the "
"purchase decision, while $x1$ relates more to brand exposure."
msgstr ""
"¿Afectará esto a todos nuestros canales de la misma manera? Probablemente"
" no. Nuestros competidores pueden no impactar nuestra notoriedad de "
"marca, pero probablemente influyen en la consideración de nuestros "
"clientes. Podríamos pensar que $x2$ está más afectado por nuestros "
"competidores que $x1$. Esto se debe a que $x2$ está más cerca de la "
"decisión de compra, mientras que $x1$ se relaciona más con la exposición "
"de la marca."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560008
#: b1f64160674f4eac8ea95446fff99b7a
msgid ""
"This suggests that ‘competitor_offers’ might be an unseen factor "
"affecting $x2$ but not $x1$. Formally, this means we could express $x2$ "
"as a function of ‘competitor_offers’ while $x1$ would not include this "
"factor."
msgstr ""
"Esto sugiere que ‘competitor_offers’ podría ser un factor no visible que "
"afecta a $x2$ pero no a $x1$. Formalmente, esto significa que podríamos "
"expresar $x2$ como una función de ‘competitor_offers’ mientras que $x1$ "
"no incluiría este factor."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560010
#: 7cc835c6ded24c04ac3d9c9e971f8e3e
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"x2 = f(competitor\\_offers) + f(x1) + f(Spend_{x2}) + f(holiday\\_signal)"
" + \\epsilon\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"x2 = f(competitor\\_offers) + f(x1) + f(Spend_{x2}) + f(holiday\\_signal) + \\epsilon\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560014
#: ceb19d6d891144d0891a16db6a9cf6a2
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"x1 = f(Spend_{x1}) + f(holiday\\_signal) + \\epsilon\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"x1 = f(Spend_{x1}) + f(holiday\\_signal) + \\epsilon\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560018
#: 6db9140f8dc14317ac3e01969408263a
msgid ""
"This is a good approach for building our model. However, we need to add "
"‘competitor_offers’ to our model, and we currently have no data on our "
"competitors, so we need to think creatively."
msgstr ""
"Este es un buen enfoque para construir nuestro modelo. Sin embargo, "
"necesitamos añadir ‘competitor_offers’ a nuestro modelo, y actualmente no"
" tenemos datos sobre nuestros competidores, por lo que necesitamos pensar"
" de manera creativa."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560020
#: be3c7874d8fb4b26b493e3ba7b37ce0d
msgid "Using Gaussian Process to Model Competitor Offers"
msgstr "Uso de Procesos Gaussianos para Modelar Ofertas de Competidores"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560022
#: e6237e1201694d9d98c2fb71e4d0dd39
msgid ""
"Since we do not directly observe competitor activities like offers or "
"discounts, we can treat ‘competitor_offers’ as a **hidden variable**. "
"This means we will not measure it directly but will infer its behavior "
"based on its impact on other variables in our model. A **Gaussian Process"
" (GP)** can help us model this hidden factor, as it is flexible enough to"
" reflect the data's underlying patterns."
msgstr ""
"Dado que no observamos directamente las actividades de los competidores, "
"como ofertas o descuentos, podemos tratar ‘competitor_offers’ como una "
"**variable oculta**. Esto significa que no la mediremos directamente, "
"sino que inferiremos su comportamiento en función de su impacto en otras "
"variables de nuestro modelo. Un **Proceso Gaussiano (GP)** puede "
"ayudarnos a modelar este factor oculto, ya que es lo suficientemente "
"flexible para reflejar los patrones subyacentes de los datos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560024
#: 1138109fbf68421b81c0551be113e65e
msgid "A Gaussian Process can be expressed as:"
msgstr "Un Proceso Gaussiano puede expresarse como:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560026
#: ef3e38eb9a164c6bb847d85e6c4eb65f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"f(t) \\sim \\mathcal{GP}(m(t), k(t, t'))\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"f(t) \\sim \\mathcal{GP}(m(t), k(t, t'))\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560031
#: 8e98d40e864f45638d3ea60e6beaeef1
msgid "$f(t)$: The hidden function representing ‘competitor_offers’ over time."
msgstr ""
"$f(t)$: La función oculta que representa ‘competitor_offers’ a lo largo "
"del tiempo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560032
#: 79dbd803eacc4fc592c75495f1ed70b2
msgid ""
"$m(t)$: The mean function, often set to 0 unless we have prior knowledge "
"of a specific trend."
msgstr ""
"$m(t)$: La función media, a menudo establecida en 0 a menos que tengamos "
"conocimiento previo de una tendencia específica."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560033
#: 28e8998702c04a7f911b7d25b01b9ded
msgid ""
"$k(t, t')$: The covariance function (or kernel), which determines the "
"smoothness and structure of $f(t)$."
msgstr ""
"$k(t, t')$: La función de covarianza (o núcleo), que determina la "
"suavidad y la estructura de $f(t)$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560035
#: c41efafe075a455694b5e903bae0be9a
msgid ""
"PyMC-Marketing includes Gaussian Processes, using a **Hilbert Space "
"Gaussian Process (HSGP) approximation** to make calculations more "
"manageable. This allows us to approximate the hidden function $f(t)$ "
"efficiently."
msgstr ""
"PyMC-Marketing incluye Procesos Gaussianos, utilizando una **aproximación"
" de Proceso Gaussiano en Espacio de Hilbert (HSGP)** para hacer que los "
"cálculos sean más manejables. Esto nos permite aproximar la función "
"oculta $f(t)$ de manera eficiente."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560037
#: 2f581f99f8c54e2692d36acfe85c7033
msgid "Why Use a Gaussian Process?"
msgstr "¿Por qué utilizar un proceso gaussiano?"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560039
#: 7c178d4e801249f8b2725156ec3e005a
msgid ""
"Reveal the hidden structure of ‘competitor_offers’ and other unobserved "
"variables based on its connections to $x2$ and other observed variables."
msgstr ""
"Revele la estructura oculta de ‘competitor_offers’ y otras variables no "
"observadas basadas en sus conexiones con $x2$ y otras variables "
"observadas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560040
#: 81fee6b6822e44bcb9746c7244ac3712
msgid ""
"Capture non-linear, varying effects that may arise from unseen competitor"
" activities."
msgstr ""
"Capture efectos no lineales y variables que pueden surgir de actividades "
"de competidores no visibles."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:560042
#: 92f203977ca4490d90848dfe26b41a82
msgid "Now let's see how we can implement this in PyMC-Marketing!"
msgstr "Ahora veamos cómo podemos implementar esto en PyMC-Marketing."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:590002
#: a13a16c9e06b42bf9f9333ac0a97eb2b
msgid ""
"Let’s delve into the output. First, it’s important to note that our "
"adjustment set clearly indicates the need to control for both "
"**competitors** and **holidays** to accurately estimate our variables. "
"This implies that the variables in our regressions should include those "
"factors along with our treatment variables. Since we lack any observed "
"variables in the data to account for competitors, we set the parameter "
"`time_varying_intercept` to `True` so that our model can accommodate the "
"unobserved confounder."
msgstr ""
"Profundicemos en la salida. Primero, es importante señalar que nuestro "
"conjunto de ajustes indica claramente la necesidad de controlar tanto por"
" **competidores** como por **días festivos** para estimar con precisión "
"nuestras variables. Esto implica que las variables en nuestras "
"regresiones deben incluir esos factores junto con nuestras variables de "
"tratamiento. Dado que no contamos con ninguna variable observada en los "
"datos para tener en cuenta a los competidores, establecemos el parámetro "
"`time_varying_intercept` en `True` para que nuestro modelo pueda acomodar"
" el confusor no observado."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:590004
#: 6330a462e59348f5b359a18b3640d4e5
msgid "Now, let’s take a look at how well our model fits."
msgstr "Ahora, echemos un vistazo a qué tan bien se ajusta nuestro modelo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:630002
#: 0db43b5ef9014578921213bb06cfbd6a
msgid ""
"Great compared to the previous models, we don't have any divergencies, as"
" we discussed before thats a good signal 🔥."
msgstr ""
"Excelente en comparación con los modelos anteriores, no tenemos ninguna "
"divergencia, como discutimos antes, eso es una buena señal 🔥."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:630004
#: 58017ab9f8784df4bafa6b09fca688ad
msgid ""
"Lets observe the recovered effect of our treatment variables ($x1$ and "
"$x2$) and as usual the not so causal model fit 👀"
msgstr ""
"Observemos el efecto recuperado de nuestras variables de tratamiento "
"($x1$ y $x2$) y, como de costumbre, el ajuste del modelo que no es tan "
"causal 👀"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:660002
#: 8da3763e67b84a47bdccbb7e40f6f8f8
msgid ""
"Great news! 🎉 Our model is nailing it when it comes to figuring out the "
"actual impact of our treatment variables. We managed to take into account"
" both the unseen confounders and the things we can see, like holidays."
msgstr ""
"¡Grandes noticias! 🎉 Nuestro modelo está logrando un excelente desempeño "
"al determinar el impacto real de nuestras variables de tratamiento. Hemos"
" conseguido tener en cuenta tanto los factores de confusión no visibles "
"como las cosas que podemos ver, como los días festivos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:660004
#: 39767d2d929d44dcb4813f899775ea86
msgid ""
"You might have noticed we have variables like market growth that aren’t "
"in the data—what's going on with that? Before diving in, let’s observe "
"the time-varying intercept."
msgstr ""
"Es posible que haya notado que tenemos variables como el crecimiento del "
"mercado que no están en los datos—¿qué está sucediendo con eso? Antes de "
"profundizar, observemos el intercepto variable en el tiempo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:680002
#: 9e85b3e6d7974c5c9866d55f7d448e49
msgid ""
"This intercept is really good at picking up on that unobserved confounder"
" and the effect of market growth. Essentially, the Gaussian process is "
"smart enough to guess all those hidden variables affecting our outcome."
msgstr ""
"Este intercepto es realmente bueno para captar ese confusor no observado "
"y el efecto del crecimiento del mercado. Esencialmente, el proceso "
"gaussiano es lo suficientemente inteligente como para adivinar todas esas"
" variables ocultas que afectan nuestro resultado."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:680004
#: 56400ba9912e4e22887d3916552973aa
msgid ""
"Since we have a solid grasp of our context, we can identify which "
"variables our Gaussian process is figuring out. This insight helps us "
"fine-tune our model. On the flip side, if we didn’t understand our world "
"well, the Gaussian process might be inferring the wrong variables, "
"leading to incorrect conclusions. That’s why it’s crucial to really "
"understand our causal ecosystem, the world around us, and how our causal "
"relationships are structured. Every choice and assumption we make with "
"our models can complicate things, impacting the accuracy of our results."
msgstr ""
"Dado que tenemos una comprensión sólida de nuestro contexto, podemos "
"identificar qué variables está determinando nuestro proceso gaussiano. "
"Esta información nos ayuda a ajustar nuestro modelo. Por otro lado, si no"
" entendemos bien nuestro mundo, el proceso gaussiano podría estar "
"inferiendo las variables incorrectas, lo que llevaría a conclusiones "
"erróneas. Por eso es crucial entender realmente nuestro ecosistema "
"causal, el mundo que nos rodea y cómo están estructuradas nuestras "
"relaciones causales. Cada elección y suposición que hacemos con nuestros "
"modelos puede complicar las cosas, impactando la precisión de nuestros "
"resultados."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:680006
#: a8533b5600ba4ebf960c3532f7536d6d
msgid ""
"We shouldn’t complicate our model without a solid reason. Adding new "
"variables or Gaussian processes should be carefully considered! It’s "
"essential to grasp the consequences of our choices and the assumptions we"
" adopt once we make them. Using causal identification techniques can help"
" us figure out which control variables to include, guiding us in the "
"causal discovery journey."
msgstr ""
"No deberíamos complicar nuestro modelo sin una razón sólida. ¡Agregar "
"nuevas variables o procesos gaussianos debe ser considerado con cuidado! "
"Es esencial comprender las consecuencias de nuestras elecciones y las "
"suposiciones que adoptamos una vez que las hacemos. Utilizar técnicas de "
"identificación causal puede ayudarnos a determinar qué variables de "
"control incluir, guiándonos en el viaje de descubrimiento causal."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:680008
#: d16534322c6b4264b104b152ab7764b6
msgid "Wrap-Up"
msgstr "Resumen"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:680010
#: 35ced164548d43538a43563dfe9c442e
msgid ""
"In this notebook, we explored how to use causal discovery methods to spot"
" unobserved confounders and how to use adjustment sets for including "
"control variables. We also looked at how Gaussian processes can help us "
"model these hidden confounders, particularly through the time-varying "
"intercept."
msgstr ""
"En este cuaderno, exploramos cómo utilizar métodos de descubrimiento "
"causal para identificar confusores no observados y cómo emplear conjuntos"
" de ajuste para incluir variables de control. También analizamos cómo los"
" procesos gaussianos pueden ayudarnos a modelar estos confusores ocultos,"
" particularmente a través del intercepto variable en el tiempo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_causal_identification.ipynb:680012
#: 346a35e90ed743e49a54562c72e8ae9d
msgid "Now it’s your turn—go ahead and start building your own models!"
msgstr "Ahora es tu turno: ¡adelante y comienza a construir tus propios modelos!"

